{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Generation.</b> Now he explains the meaning of 'and greatly praised,' [namely] that the generation that passed on will recount to the coming generation your deeds; 'they will tell' — both generations." "And the meaning of 'and your might' — for among the praises of a king is his being mighty."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:48.948996085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}